### Requirements

- **Atomic.** One skill, tool or duty per entry. A posting line reading
  "Experience with Docker, Kubernetes and Terraform" is three requirements, not
  one.
- **`kind` comes from the posting's own sectioning**, not from your judgement of
  importance: `must` under requirements/qualifications/"what you'll need",
  `nice` under nice-to-have/preferred/bonus, `responsibility` under
  responsibilities/"what you'll do".
- **`terms` are the technology and skill words the requirement names, written
  in the candidate's vocabulary** (the list below) whenever the posting is
  talking about something on it. "Solid grasp of K8s" gives
  `["Kubernetes"]`{% if vocabulary %}; "Azure Kubernetes Services (AKS)" names more than one thing,
  so it gives every entry it names{% endif %}. Use the posting's own word only when nothing on
  the list means the same thing — an unmatched term is a real gap and must not
  be replaced by the nearest thing on the list. Leave the list empty when a
  requirement names no technology at all.
- **`surface` is the posting's own spelling** of the same things, in the same
  order — `["K8s"]`, `["Azure Kubernetes Services (AKS)"]`. Omit it, or leave
  it empty, when the posting spelled them the way `terms` does.
- **`weight`** is between 0.5 and 1.5 and defaults to 1.0. Use it only when the
  posting itself insists ("must have", "critical") or hedges ("exposure to",
  "any of").
- **`category`** is the candidate category (below) the requirement belongs to,
  or null when it belongs to none of them.
- Skip pure company marketing, benefits, and equal-opportunity boilerplate.
  Aim for at most {{ max_requirements }} requirements.

### Gates

Gates are hard filters. For each one give the verdict, and when the posting says
something about it, **quote the posting verbatim** in `quote` (one sentence).

- `eligibility` — citizenship, permanent residency, security clearance, work
  passes, right to work. `fail` when the posting restricts who may apply.
- `language` — a natural language the posting requires{% if languages %} beyond {{ languages|join(", ") }}{% endif %}.
  `fail` when it requires one, `pass` when it does not. A programming language
  is never a language gate.
- `location` — relocation, on-site or in-office requirements. `flag` when the
  posting constrains where the work happens.
- `deadline` — a closing date. Put the ISO date (`YYYY-MM-DD`) in `date`.
  {% if today %}Today is {{ today }}; `fail` when the date has passed.{% endif %}
- `seniority` — years of experience or a senior title. `flag` when the posting
  asks for more than a student or new graduate can have.

Use `unknown` when the posting says nothing at all about a gate, and never
invent a quote: `quote` is either text copied from the posting or null.

